unit, so the emblem reaches Elderwood 7 a level before Gnar; without a Spatula it still works one Elderwood step lower. It shares Aphelios with Nidalee Aphelios, one of the most played boards at Diamond and above, so scout for Aphelios players before 4-1.\nL31: ## Units and items\nL32: \nL33:   * cite27†Image: Aphelios cite28†Aphelios Carry\nL34:   * cite29†Image: Ezreal cite30†Ezreal Carry\nL35:   * cite31†Image: Lillia cite32†Lillia No items needed\nL36:   * cite33†Image: Hecarim cite34†Hecarim L37:   * cite35†Image: LeBlanc cite36†LeBlanc No items needed\nL38:   * cite37†Image: Alistar cite38†Alistar No items needed\nL39:   * cite39†Image: Ornn cite40†Ornn No items needed\nL40:   * cite41†Image: Xayah cite42†Xayah No items needed\nL41: Aphelios carries with Elderwood Emblem, Guinsoo's Rageblade and Kraken's Fury. Ezreal carries with Deathblade, Infinity Edge and Spear of Shojin. Hecarim takes Evenshroud, Protector's Vow and Sunfire Cape.\nL42: ### Item order\nL43: \nL44:   1. cite18†Image: Elderwood Emblem Elderwood Emblem\nL45:   2. cite19†Image: Guinsoo's Rageblade Guinsoo's Rageblade\nL46:   3. cite24†Image: Infinity Edge Infinity Edge\nL47:   4. cite20†Image: Kraken's Fury Kraken's Fury\nL48:   5. cite12†Image: Evenshroud Evenshroud\nL49: \nL50: ## How to play Elderwood Aphelios\nL51: ### Early game\nL52: \nL53: Elderwood openers (Ornn, Xayah, Alistar, LeBlanc) are steady; hold Bows and Swords and a Spatula for the emblem.\nL54: \nL55:   * cite39†Image: Ornn Ornn\nL56:   * cite41†Image: Xayah Xayah\nL57:   * cite37†Image: Alistar Alistar\nL58:   * cite35†Image: LeBlanc LeBlanc\nL59: \nL60: ### Mid game\nL61: \nL62: Level 8 at 4-1 and roll for Aphelios and Ezreal at two stars.\nL63: ### Late game\nL64: \nL65: At level 9, Gnar joins the front line and makes Brawler 2 with Alistar.\nL66: \nL67: TipAphelios takes the Elderwood Emblem, Guinsoo's and Kraken's Fury; Ezreal Deathblade, Infinity Edge and Shojin; Hecarim Evenshroud, Protector's Vow and Sunfire Cape. Keep LeBlanc on the board for the sixth Elderwood unit even when a stronger unit is offered.\nL68: ## Best augments\nL69: \nL70:   * cite43†Image: Spreading Roots cite44†Spreading Roots Gold, S tier on our list Gain a random Emblems. After 3 combats, gain another.\nL71:   * cite45†Image: Branching Out cite46†Branching Out Silver, S tier on our list Gain a random Emblem.\nL72:   * cite47†Image: Swordsmith cite48†Swordsmith Gold, A tier on our list Gain 2 random completed items that build from B.F. Sword.\nL73:   * cite49†Image: Latent Forge cite50†Latent Forge Silver, S tier on our list After 8 player combats, gain an Artifact anvil.\nL74: Augment priority: emblems, then items.\nL75: ## Traits\nL76: \nL77: cite51†Image: Elderwood Elderwood 7cite52†Image: Rapidfire Rapidfire 2cite53†Image: Fae Fae 2cite54†Image: Defender Defender 2\nL78: \nL79: Active on the final board: 7 Elderwood, 2 Rapidfire, 2 Fae and 2 Defender. Every trait is explained in the cite55†Set 18 traits guide .\nL80: \nL81: ## Late upgrades\nL82: \nL83:   * cite56†Image: Gnar Gnar added\nL84: \nL85: ## Questions about Elderwood Aphelios\nL86: ### Is Elderwood Aphelios good in patch 18.4b?\nL87: \nL88: Elderwood Aphelios is S tier on the PivotTFT comp tier list for patch 18.4b: one of the strongest and most consistent comps this patch, worth steering towards from most openings.\nL89: \nL90: ### Who is the carry in Elderwood Aphelios?\nL91: \nL92: Aphelios is the main carry. Build Elderwood Emblem, Guinsoo's Rageblade and Kraken's Fury on Aphelios.\nL93: ### What level do you play Elderwood Aphelios at?\nL94: \nL95: Elderwood Aphelios is a Fast 8 comp: you save gold, level to 8 quickly and roll there for the 4-cost carries. Roll for the board at level 8.\nL96: \nL97: ### How do I import Elderwood Aphelios into TFT?\nL98: \nL99: Copy its team code with the button on this page, then open the Team Planner in the TFT client and paste it.\nL100: ### What are the best augments for Elderwood Aphelios?\nL101: \nL102: Spreading Roots, Branching Out, Swordsmith and Latent Forge. When none of these is offered, take emblems, then items augments.\nL103: \nL104: ## Similar comps\nL105: \nL106:   * cite57†SAlune Fast 9 L107:   * cite58†SFlora Azir Reroll L108:   * cite59†SKha'Zix Reroll L109: ## More comps for patch 18.4b\nL110: \nL111: S\nL112: \nL113:   * cite57†Alune Fast 9 L114:   * cite58†Flora Azir Reroll L115:   * cite59†Kha'Zix Reroll L116:   * cite60†Nidalee Aphelios L117:   * cite61†Rapidfire Aphelios L118:   * cite62†Riftbeast Reroll L119:   * cite63†Veigar Reroll L120: \nL121: A\nL122:   * cite64†Akali Camille Reroll L123:   * cite65†Coven Morgana L124:   * cite66†Draven Fast 9 L125:   * cite67†Elder Dragon Fast 9 L126:   * cite68†Elderwood Ezreal L127:   * cite69†Elderwood Teemo Reroll L128:   * cite70†Executioner Ezreal Ahri L129:   * cite71†Invoker Ahri Morgana L130:   * cite72†Invoker Teemo Reroll L131:   * cite73†Lunar Kayle L132:   * cite74†Master Yi Reroll L133:   * cite75†Rengar Master Yi Reroll L134:   * cite76†Riftbeast 10 L135:   * cite77†Warwick Reroll L136: \nL137: B\nL138:   * cite78†Aphelios Vanguard L139:   * cite79†Ashe Fast 9 L140:   * cite80†Azir Reroll L141:   * cite81†Blackthorn Veigar L142:   * cite82†Blossom Ahri L143:   * cite83†Blossom Ahri Fast 9 L144:   * cite84†Blossom Ashe Fast 9 L145:   * cite85†Blossom Elder Dragon Fast 9 L146:   * cite86†Cassiopeia Reroll L147:   * cite87†Executioner Fast 9 L148:   * cite88†Executioner Yunara Reroll L149:   * cite89†Flora Malphite L150:   * cite90†Invoker Kog'Maw L151:   * cite91†Invoker Morgana L152:   * cite92†Invoker Nidalee L153:   * cite93†Juggernaut Zyra L154:   * cite94†Juggernaut Zyra Nidalee L155:   * cite95†Kayle Reroll L156:   * cite96†Lunar Aphelios Fa